    {
      "id": "frame_c91a414a90096a9bf6",
      "type": "section",
      "text": "TCP Slow Start",
      "active_visual_id": null,
      "page_number": 1,
      "auto_advance_allowed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "frame_1b893a9f959c8efd4c",
      "type": "causal",
      "text": "TCP begins with a small congestion window because the sender does not yet know the path capacity.",
      "active_visual_id": null,
      "page_number": 1,
      "auto_advance_allowed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "frame_1ce05e424c00daa3d7",
      "type": "proposition",
      "text": "Each acknowledged round increases the amount of data in flight, so growth is initially exponential.",
      "active_visual_id": null,
      "page_number": 1,
      "auto_advance_allowed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "frame_4021fd868810671dea",
      "type": "proposition",
      "text": "When loss occurs, the sender reduces the window and records a threshold for later additive increase.",
      "active_visual_id": null,
      "page_number": 1,
      "auto_advance_allowed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "frame_755b212c48e9c31725",
      "type": "contrast",
      "text": "However, a timeout does not prove that every packet was lost; it is a conservative congestion signal.",
      "active_visual_id": null,
      "page_number": 1,
      "auto_advance_allowed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "frame_1c1b6ed5ae06b5fc62",
      "type": "section",
      "text": "2.",
